1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Lincoln's head, a borrowed body

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
Guess whose body it is

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,800
It's B: John C. Calhoun

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,000
He said slavery wasn't an evil, but a good

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,200
The Emancipator's head on a pro-slavery body

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,400
Even the papers on the desk were rewritten

7
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,800
That was only the first

8
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,000
The second stars Lincoln's widow

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,200
She gave a false name; he said he didn't know her

10
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:35,200
A pair of hands on her shoulders

11
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:40,000
Behind her stands "Lincoln"

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,200
He had been tried for fraud in 1869, and walked free

13
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:46,400
How he did it is still unclear

14
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:49,600
The usual trick for ghosts: double exposure

15
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,800
Same plate, exposed a second time

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,000
Another kind of fake: a composite

17
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,200
Only the head is Grant's

18
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,500
So who made the third Lincoln?

19
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,200
The third was made by a magician, to expose the fakers

20
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,400
Houdini promised his wife a code from beyond

21
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,600
He died on Halloween; she held séances for 10 years

22
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:16,800
At the last one, nothing came

23
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:20,000
This Halloween marks 100 years since he died

24
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,600
It's wanting to believe that fools you

25
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,000
What's the last picture that fooled you?

26
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,600
Lincoln's head, a borrowed body